-- title:
--   Snapper induction step: first difference of twisted Euler characteristics
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $V$ a scheme and $\pi\colon V\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ a proper morphism; let $K$ be an ordered affine cover of $V$, that is, a finite linearly ordered index type $K.\iota$ together with opens $U_i\subseteq V$, each affine, with $\bigsqcup_i U_i=\top$. Let $L$ be an $\mathcal O_V$-module (an object of `V.Modules`) which is locally trivial in the sense that every point of $V$ lies in an open $U$ for which the pullback of $L$ along the inclusion $U\hookrightarrow V$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules on $U$, and let $s\colon\mathbf 1\to L$ be a morphism from the monoidal unit. Let $Z_0$ be a closed subset of $V$ with $Z_0\neq\emptyset$ such that the closed subscheme cut out by the vanishing ideal sheaf data of $Z_0$ is integral, and assume $Z_0$ is not contained in the support of `Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal s`, the smallest ideal sheaf datum $J$ on $V$ with $J.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ containing, for each affine open $U$, the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s$ on $U$. Then there exist a closed subset $Y_1$ of $V$ with $Y_1<Z_0$ in the lattice of closed sets and $Y_1$ contained in the support of `Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal s`, and a presheaf of $\mathcal O_V$-modules datum $G_1$ over $\pi$ which is coherent (each $G_1(U)$ is a finite $\Gamma(V,U)$-module for $U$ affine open), quasi-coherent (on each affine open $U$ and each $f\in\Gamma(V,U)$, every section over the basic open $V_f$ is $f^{-n}$ times the restriction of a section over $U$, and a section over $U$ restricting to $0$ on $V_f$ is killed by some $f^n$) and supported in $Y_1$ (i.e. $G_1(U)$ is a subsingleton whenever the affine open $U$ is disjoint from $Y_1$), such that for every $n\in\mathbb N$ $$\chi_K\bigl(\iota_*\mathcal O_{Z_0}\otimes L^{\otimes(n+1)}\bigr)-\chi_K\bigl(\iota_*\mathcal O_{Z_0}\otimes L^{\otimes n}\bigr)=\chi_K\bigl(G_1\otimes L^{\otimes(n+1)}\bigr),$$ where $\iota$ is the closed immersion of the subscheme of the vanishing ideal of $Z_0$ and $\iota_*\mathcal O_{Z_0}$ denotes `OModulePresheaf.pushforwardUnit`, $L^{\otimes m}$ is `Scheme.Modules.tensorPow` (the unit for $m=0$ and $L^{\otimes m}\otimes L$ for $m+1$), the twist is the open-by-open tensor product with $L^{\otimes m}$, and $\chi_K(F)=\sum_{i<\#K.\iota}(-1)^i\,\mathrm{cechFinrank}_i(F,K)$.
--
--   This is the inductive step of the Snapper–Kleiman argument on the numerical behaviour of Čech Euler characteristics of twists: multiplication by the section $s$ relates the twisted Euler characteristics of the integral closed subscheme $Z_0$ at consecutive exponents, the discrepancy being accounted for by a coherent datum supported on the strictly smaller closed set $Z_0\cap Z(s)$. It is used in the proof that the twisted Euler characteristic is a polynomial function of bounded degree, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.OModulePresheaf.degree_lt_of_forall_eulerChar_twist_tensorPow_eq_of_inter_iInter_support_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_empty`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.OModulePresheaf.degree_lt_of_forall_eulerChar_twist_tensorPow_eq_of_inter_iInter_support_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_empty).
